            <section class="content-section" id="stockrooms">
                <h2 class="section-title">Stockrooms (<code>alm_stockroom</code>)</h2>
                <div class="prose">
                    <p>
                        A <strong>Stockroom</strong> is a physical or logical location where assets are stored when they are not in use. This could be a massive central warehouse, or a small IT closet in a regional office.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        When an asset is assigned to a stockroom, its State is typically <code>In Stock</code> and its Substate might be <code>Available</code> or <code>Reserved</code>.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="content-section" id="stock-rules">
                <h2 class="section-title">Automated Restocking via Stock Rules</h2>
                <div class="prose">
                    <p>
                        HAM Pro can automate inventory management using <strong>Stock Rules</strong>. A stock rule watches a specific Stockroom for a specific Model (e.g., "Watch the London Office for MacBook Pros").
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        If the quantity falls below the <strong>Threshold</strong>, the rule can automatically trigger one of two actions:
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Vendor Order:</strong> Automatically generates a Purchase Order to buy more from a vendor.</li>
                        <li><strong>Transfer:</strong> Automatically generates a Transfer Order to pull stock from a parent warehouse.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="content-section" id="transfer-orders">
                <h2 class="section-title">Transfer Orders (<code>alm_transfer_order</code>)</h2>
                <div class="prose">
                    <p>
                        When you need to move an asset from one stockroom to another (e.g., from the Central Warehouse to the New York Office), you use a <strong>Transfer Order</strong>.
                    </p>
                </div>
                
                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="mermaid">
                    stateDiagram-v2
                        direction TB
                        
                        Draft --> Requested
                        Requested --> Shipment_Prep
                        Shipment_Prep --> In_Transit
                        In_Transit --> Received
                        
                        note right of Draft
                            Select Source & Dest Stockrooms
                        end note
                        note right of In_Transit
                            Asset state changes to "In Transit"
                        end note
                        note right of Received
                            Asset state changes back to "In Stock", new Stockroom assigned
                        end note
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>
